      "writtenOn": "2022-04-28T04:53:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e if the load is high and use_high_wq it may take a while to get here.\n\nMaybe, but I would bet a bigger change. Like said, I think we may want a kthread which can inherit the caller\u0027s scheduling priority/policy but at this moment we probably would prefer a smaller code change for T (so I cleaned out the WQ for api_ver \u003c TRUSTY_API_VERSION_SMP_NOP for such reason).\n\n\nI never see this for our usage, as we toggle this in user space before trusty execution. For the cases then trust is already running, the delay is happened just between trusty (trusty_std_call32 \u003d\u003d\u003e SM_ERR_NOP_INTERRUPTED) interrupted by IRQ till we reach the nice adjustment. Normally I see we have many many small scheduling delays, so even if we miss the first time, it is still a big improvement.\n\nAlso",
      "parentUuid": "83507eae_616ac247",
      "revId": "16f39a3a7874753fc2e2db2ae09141cea7a3b4c7",
